1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:01,688
BRAMBLE: Case open!

2
00:00:01,688 --> 00:00:04,460
OTTO: Oh no! The till won't balance!

3
00:00:04,660 --> 00:00:07,952
IVY: The sheet and the money don't match.

4
00:00:08,352 --> 00:00:11,821
Today's case: the till that won't balance.

5
00:00:12,121 --> 00:00:16,161
Regroup means swapping ten ones for one ten.

6
00:00:16,561 --> 00:00:21,363
Like ten one-dollar coins for a ten-dollar note.

7
00:00:21,963 --> 00:00:24,980
The till started with 38 dollars.

8
00:00:25,180 --> 00:00:29,164
Then it sold 27 dollars of icy poles.

9
00:00:29,564 --> 00:00:34,093
OTTO: Eight and seven make fifteen. Write the five!

10
00:00:34,293 --> 00:00:37,651
OTTO: Three and two make five. 55 dollars!

11
00:00:38,051 --> 00:00:41,046
IVY: Hmm. Where did the ten go?

12
00:00:41,446 --> 00:00:44,212
BRAMBLE: Let's not guess. Let's test.

13
00:00:44,612 --> 00:00:48,235
BRAMBLE: Can you point to the one-dollar coins?

14
00:00:51,335 --> 00:00:54,344
BRAMBLE: How much should be in the till?

15
00:00:54,744 --> 00:00:56,980
A. 55 dollars.

16
00:00:57,180 --> 00:00:59,672
B. 65 dollars.

17
00:00:59,872 --> 00:01:01,784
Pause and think.

18
00:01:06,384 --> 00:01:10,833
Ten ones and one ten are worth the same.

19
00:01:11,233 --> 00:01:14,368
Eight and seven make fifteen ones.

20
00:01:14,768 --> 00:01:17,861
Swap ten ones for one ten.

21
00:01:18,461 --> 00:01:22,638
Now there are six tens and five ones.

22
00:01:23,038 --> 00:01:25,504
It's B! 65 dollars.

23
00:01:25,704 --> 00:01:28,757
OTTO: Oh! I forgot the swapped ten!

24
00:01:29,157 --> 00:01:31,464
BRAMBLE: Let's check another way.

25
00:01:31,664 --> 00:01:37,141
65 take away 27. Swap a ten for ten ones.

26
00:01:37,541 --> 00:01:43,253
Fifteen take away seven is eight. Five take away two is three.

27
00:01:43,653 --> 00:01:46,532
IVY: 38! Now the till balances!

28
00:01:46,932 --> 00:01:48,240
BRAMBLE: Case solved!

29
00:01:49,740 --> 00:01:51,738
OTTO: I'll carry the ten!

30
00:01:52,138 --> 00:01:54,618
IVY: Not like a surfboard, Otto!

31
00:01:55,218 --> 00:02:00,007
Remember. Ten ones and one ten are worth the same.

32
00:02:00,507 --> 00:02:06,740
Say it with me. Ten ones and one ten are worth the same.

33
00:02:08,540 --> 00:02:13,868
Try it at home. Bundle ten pegs to make one ten.

34
00:02:14,368 --> 00:02:18,199
Next case: ladybird dots at a glance.

